program scoped_charges

-- ============================================================
-- Scoped charges: the record picks the figure's source
-- ============================================================
--
-- A tariff prices many kinds of charge, and not every charge takes
-- its quantity from the same place. A metered charge is priced off
-- what the meter itself recorded - the caller has no say in the
-- figure. A caller-sourced charge is priced off the quantity the
-- caller proposes - a negotiated block, a contracted allowance -
-- because there is nothing in the record to read it from. Which
-- source applies is not the caller's choice either: the tariff
-- declares it, once, per charge.
--
-- The trap in most billing systems is that this selection lives in
-- application code: an if-statement in the billing engine decides
-- which figure to apply, and nothing stops a bug - or a caller -
-- from applying a proposed figure to a metered charge. Here the
-- selection is part of the record's own law. One line act serves
-- every source, and the applied figure is computed by the rules
-- from the source the tariff declares: if(...) picks the meter's
-- own reading for a metered charge and the caller's proposal
-- otherwise, in the act AND in the invariant that re-checks every
-- committed line. A line wearing the wrong source's figure cannot
-- commit, and no future source multiplies the acts.
--
-- Before the conditional this was two acts - a record-quantity act
-- and a caller-quantity act - duplicating their shared body, with
-- every new source adding another copy. The deletion is the point:
-- this example is the embedder's five-bodies collapse in miniature.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- The claims
-- ------------------------------------------------------------

-- The tariff's declaration: which source prices this charge. The
-- charge determines its source - one declaration, no rewrites.
predicate TariffCharge(charge: Subject, source: Subject)
    unique by (charge)
    append only

-- What the meter itself recorded. Append only and unique by the
-- meter: one standing reading per meter in this single-period
-- snapshot, and a reading does not unhappen.
predicate MeterReading(meter: Subject, qty: Decimal)
    unique by (meter)
    append only

-- One priced line. It keeps BOTH figures: what the caller proposed,
-- and what the record applied. For a caller-sourced charge the two
-- agree; for a metered charge the applied figure is the meter's, and
-- the proposal is on the record for what it was - a proposal.
predicate ChargeLine(line: Subject, charge: Subject, meter: Subject, proposed_qty: Decimal, applied_qty: Decimal)
    unique by (line)
    append only

-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- The rules
-- ------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every line names a charge the tariff declares - the totality
-- companion that keeps the selection below from passing emptily.
invariant lines_name_a_declared_charge:
    ChargeLine(_, charge, _, _, _) implies TariffCharge(charge, _)

-- A source the rules do not know is refused at the declaration, so
-- the selection can never meet a third case it has no branch for.
invariant sources_are_the_known_two:
    TariffCharge(_, source) implies (source = #meter or source = #caller)

-- The selection itself, re-checked over every committed line: the
-- applied figure IS the declared source's figure. For a metered
-- charge that is the meter's own reading; otherwise the caller's
-- proposal. The conditional evaluates only the branch the source
-- selects, so a caller-sourced line needs no meter reading at all.
invariant applied_quantity_follows_the_declared_source:
    ChargeLine(_, charge, meter, proposed_qty, applied_qty) and TariffCharge(charge, source)
    implies applied_qty = if(source = #meter, value MeterReading(meter, _), proposed_qty)

-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- The acts
-- ------------------------------------------------------------

transformation declare_charge(charge, source):
    admit TariffCharge(charge, source)

transformation read_meter(meter, qty):
    admit MeterReading(meter, qty)

-- The ONE line act. It looks up the charge's declared source, gates
-- on the selected source actually existing (a metered charge with no
-- reading is a lawful refusal, not a kernel error - and a
-- caller-sourced line needs no reading), then computes the applied
-- figure from the source the record declares. The caller proposes;
-- the record decides what applies.
transformation record_line(line, charge, meter, proposed_qty):
    bind TariffCharge(charge, source)
    require the_selected_source_exists: source = #caller or (source = #meter and MeterReading(meter, _))
    let applied_qty = if(source = #meter, value MeterReading(meter, _), proposed_qty)
    admit ChargeLine(line, charge, meter, proposed_qty, applied_qty)
